Z||000000||mblackwell||09-10-2001||10:17 AM||||I'm pretty sure my water pump has gone bad.  The car overheats and the radiator doesn't get hot, and water pours out of somewhere near the pump.  It has been leaking there for a few days, but I kept adding water and it didn't over heat.  I don't think the water is circulating at all now.<P>How hard is it to replace the pump?  I'm no mechanic, but I did manage to replace the fuel pump with  help.  Will I be able to do this?<P>How much will a new pump cost?<P>What tools will I need?  It looks like it has a bunch of Torx bolts in it.  This is an '88 Formula.<P>Ia there a trick top get the thermostat cap off?  I cant get it to move at all.  I took it off before and didn't have any trouble.  Could overheating get it stuck on there? I stopped as soon as the warning light came on. (Heat gauge doesn't work)<P>Thanks.||||reg||5
Z||000001||ray b||09-10-2001||11:40 AM||||pull the battery out.<BR>take off the rear pass wheel<BR>remove splash guard[inner wheel well]<BR>86 motor i did was all metric sized<BR>remove pulley first.<BR>i remove caps with a big channel lock pl.<BR>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd<p>[This message has been edited by ray b (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
